Description: Don't actually print screen contents on PrintScreen
 By default, urxvt sends the contents of the screen to the default
 printer whenever a user hits the PrintScreen key. This is really
 something users should have to opt in to to avoid accidentally
 leaking private data. It can be customized using the `print-pipe'
 resource.
Author: Ryan Kavanagh <rak@debian.org>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/955980
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2020-04-10
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
Index: rxvt-unicode/src/feature.h
===================================================================
